2. Ordered chain reconciliation compiles a deterministic parent-first
   recovery selection. An individually resource-excluded recovery and every
   recovery descendant are omitted, while unrelated later roots remain
   eligible. Normal reconciliation and fresh-generation fallback share this
   closure rule. Aggregate projection contradictions remain faults; ordinary
   retained-capacity pressure may still select the existing generation
